 ## Overview
-Clipping volumes restrict rendering to a specific region of space defined by a set of planar half-spaces, allowing internal structures to be revealed by discarding geometry outside the defined volume [S1]. Unlike static cropping masks, this method constructs a dynamic volume (up to 6 planes) that can be combined via intersection or union logic, functioning as a simple Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) expression [S1]. It is distinct from simple view-frustum culling as it allows arbitrary plane orientations and offsets independent of the camera, and from surface-level clipping as it operates on the volumetric data itself [S1].
